/E (The system is built around three core modules: the Student Input Module uses Java's Scanner class to capture student name, ID, and course preferences from the console. The Course Class acts as a data model storing course code, name, day, and time slot. Each Course object encapsulates attributes and exposes a display\(\) method for formatted timetable output.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (The CourseRegistration controller class manages the end-to-end flow: it initializes the Scanner, collects user input, instantiates Course objects, and stores them in an array. Registration logic validates selections and prevents time conflicts. Finally, the timetable output module iterates through registered courses and prints a structured schedule to the console.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
